# t0947 — `auto x = <METHOD call returning Result>` auto-propagates, binding the
# Ok PAYLOAD, and the user's whole `if x.is_error():` block is then SILENTLY
# DISCARDED. `gg check` is clean; the emitted code contains none of the block's
# statements.
#
# MEASURED (gg build --emit-gir on this program, pre-fix): the local is typed
# `_4: bool ; j` — the Ok payload, not the Result — and the Error basic block is
# the compiler's SYNTHESIZED propagation (`enum_init Error { copy <payload> }`),
# not the user's. Neither `print("handled")` nor `return Error("custom message")`
# appears anywhere in the GIR or the emitted C.
#
# DISCRIMINATED from the auto-propagation family already filed:
#   * a FREE call does NOT do this — `auto r = free_fn()` binds the Result and
#     the block runs (measured, same program shape).
#   * an EXPLICIT binding does NOT do this — `Result[bool, String] j = s.join(g)`
#     runs the user's block and prints the two intended lines (measured).
#   Only `auto` + a METHOD call reaches the discarding path.
#
# LIVE IN SHIPPED STDLIB: `lib/xtd/p2p.gg`'s `p2p_enable_discovery` has exactly
# this shape. It is green ONLY BY LUCK (SIX QUESTIONS #6) — its discarded block
# happens to be semantically identical to the compiler's substitute. That site
# is also the sole provenance of the 13 `p2p_*` fixtures' `type_name == None`
# fires at the method-dispatch gate (`todo/t0936`).
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): the user's error branch runs — `handled` then
# `custom message`, exactly what the explicit `Result[bool, String]` binding
# already produces today. If the owner instead rules that a var-decl `auto`
# binding SHOULD auto-propagate, then `j.is_error()` on the resulting `bool`
# must be a check-time REJECTION and this fixture flips to a negative. What is
# NOT a legal outcome either way is accepting the block and discarding it
# (Core #10, lower-or-reject).

struct Sock:
    int h

equip Sock:
    Result[bool, String] join(&self, String g):
        if g == "bad":
            return Error("runtime failure")
        return Ok(true)

Result[bool, String] enable(String group):
    Sock s = Sock(1)
    auto j = s.join(group)
    if j.is_error():
        print("handled")
        return Error("custom message")
    return Ok(true)

void main():
    auto r = enable("bad")
    if r.is_error():
        print(r.unwrap_error())
